<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive-icon FOREGROUND layer: the English-33 board in its opening position, 32 pegs
  with the centre cell (3,3) empty.

  Everything sits in one group scaled 0.69 about the canvas centre. That factor puts the
  board's true circumradius (221.2 design units) at 152.6 units = 32.2dp, inside the
  66dp adaptive safe-zone circle, so no launcher mask can clip a peg.

  Geometry is authored on the design's 512-unit canvas: cell centres are 88 + 56*index,
  dimples are radius 20, pegs radius 22 riding 6 units high, speculars are 12x8 ellipses.
  Gradient coordinates are in the same design space because the group transform applies
  to them too.

  Deliberate fidelity losses versus the design canvas: no blurred drop shadows (a vector
  has no blur primitive; launchers add their own elevation shadow), speculars are not
  rotated -25 degrees (invisible at final size, and it would cost 32 extra groups), and
  the 32 occupied-cell dimples are flat rather than inset-shaded since only their lower
  crescent shows. The centre hole keeps its two-tone inset treatment.
-->
